=== AGENTS.md ===
<!-- >>> ehai >>> -->
# ehai AI-SDLC Assistant

ehai v0.1.0-alpha.2 connects your AI harness to your GitHub Projects tracker
for product planning, task management, and UI proof-of-concepts.

## MCP server

To use ehai in any MCP-compatible harness, add this to your MCP config:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ehai": {
      "command": "ehai",
      "args": ["mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

After adding it, run `ehai doctor` to verify the connection.

## Commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `/ehai:plan [idea]` | Turn an idea into a PRD (interviews the user, Mermaid diagrams) |
| `/ehai:breakdown [prd]` | Break a PRD into epics, stories and tasks with acceptance criteria |
| `/ehai:sync [prd]` | Push an approved breakdown to the tracker (idempotent) |
| `/ehai:status` | Progress, blockers, stale work and risks |
| `/ehai:triage [report]` | Classify a bug or request and create a tracker item |
| `/ehai:assign [request]` | Assign, reassign or take a task |
| `/ehai:prefs` | Show and edit your role and preferences |
| `/ehai:help` | This overview |

## MCP tools

The `ehai` MCP server exposes: `ping`, `save_prd`, `get_plan`, `list_plans`,
`save_breakdown`, `sync_plan`, `status_report`, `triage`, `assign_task`,
`comment_task`, `team`, `guard_check`.

Resource: `ehai://prefs` — your role (`pm`/`dev`/`both`) and learned preferences.

## Data policy guardrails

This tool is designed for teams that handle sensitive data. Never put real
personally identifiable information (names with identifiers, dates of birth,
ID numbers, phone numbers, emails, or addresses) in plans, tasks, mock data
or examples. `ehai` tools check what they write and will ask if they
detect something suspicious.

Run `ehai doctor` if tools are not responding.

## End every reply with Insights

Finish every ehai reply with this footer, after any question you ask:

```
★ Insights ─────────────────────────────────────
  • <line>
  • <line>
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
```

Put 2–5 short lines in it, only the ones that help right now:

- **Summary** — what just changed, in one line (e.g. "12 tasks synced, 0 duplicates").
- **Status** — where things stand (% done, what is blocked, what is waiting on the user).
- **Next step** — the single most useful next action, with the exact command (e.g. `/ehai:sync`, `ehai poc run checkout 2`).
- **Warning** — anything risky or easy to miss (sensitive data found, stale items, a failing check). Start the line with ⚠.
- **Note / tip** — one thing that saves the user time next time.

Match the role: plain words for **pm**, commands and paths for **dev**. Use a small table inside the footer only when it is clearer than lines. Never repeat the whole reply, and never put sensitive data in it.
